<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- No GeneratePackageOnBuild: it conflicts with `dotnet pack` on a multi-targeted Razor class
         library (NU5026/NU5019 from clean) and the documented publish uses `dotnet pack -o ./nupkg`
         then `nuget push nupkg/...`, which never reads the bin/Release package anyway. -->
    <Title>Blazor Controls</Title>
    <PackageId>WssBlazorControls</PackageId>
	  <AssemblyVersion>10.8.5</AssemblyVersion>
	  <FileVersion>$(AssemblyVersion)</FileVersion>
	  <Version>$(AssemblyVersion)</Version>

    <!-- Build hygiene: the changelog promises 0 warnings — enforce it. CS1591 excepted: the public
         surface is heavily XML-documented but not exhaustively, and missing-comment noise would
         drown real warnings. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Ship the XML docs so consumers get IntelliSense from the package. -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Debuggability + reproducibility: SourceLink is built into the .NET 8+ SDK; publish the
         repo URL, ship a .snupkg symbol package, and make CI builds deterministic. -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Catches binary/source breaking changes against the previous published version at pack time. -->
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>

    <!-- Trimming / WASM AOT support. IsAotCompatible turns on IsTrimmable (the assembly-level
         [AssemblyMetadata("IsTrimmable","True")] that lets a consumer's trimmed publish actually trim
         this library) plus the trim/AOT/single-file Roslyn analyzers. With TreatWarningsAsErrors
         above, any new IL2xxx/IL3xxx regression fails the build. The reflection the library does
         (attribute reads via Field expressions, enum member lookups) is annotated or provably
         rooted — see EnumHelpers/FieldValidationDisplay for the reasoning. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <!-- Package Metadata -->
    <PackageDescription>A comprehensive library of form controls for Blazor applications, providing consistent, feature-rich input components with built-in validation, accessibility support, and flexible styling options.</PackageDescription>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <!-- SPDX expression (was PackageLicenseFile) so NuGet.org indexes/filters the license properly. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>blazor;controls;forms;validation;accessibility;ui;components;webassembly;server</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
10.8.5 -- Table column filtering gains more filter kinds, row-placed editors, and a server-side mode; data-tooltip restyled to match LabelTooltip. Additive for typical usage, with two narrow compatibility notes below for consumers using TableColumnFilter/PropertyColumn directly.

NEW
- Table filtering: Column.FilterText/TextFilterMatch (search box), Column.FilterDropdown (your own panel via TableFilterContext), FilterIcon, OnFilterDropdownOpenChange, FilterOnClose.
- PropertyColumn.Filterable/FilterValuesFromData: derive a filter from the property type, or from DataSource's distinct values, instead of declaring one by hand.
- Table.FilterPlacement = TableFilterPlacement.Row: always-visible per-column editors in a second header row, instead of funnel dropdowns.
- Table.OnFiltersChanged/ClearFiltersAsync(): the every-column counterpart to OnFilterChanged. Dropdown extras: FilterSearch, FilterCheckAll, DefaultFilterValues/FilterResetToDefault.
- Table.ClientSideFiltering = false: keeps the filter UI/events, stops the built-in row narrowing, for server-side filtering.
- Every filter label/format (FilterRowLabelFormat, FilterResultAnnouncementFormat, FilterClearLabel, FilterMinLabel/FilterMaxLabel, FilterBoolAnyText/FilterBoolTrueText/FilterBoolFalseText, FilterSelectPlaceholder, FilterSearchPlaceholder, FilterEmptyText, FilterCheckAllLabel, FilterSelectedCountFormat, FilterContainsFormat/FilterStartsWithFormat/FilterEqualsFormat, FilterDateStartLabel/FilterDateEndLabel) is a Table parameter. FilterResultAnnouncementFormat is new: a role="status" region announces it after every filter change, so an existing FilterOptions/OnFilter column gains an announcement it didn't have before -- set it to "" to silence (a null value throws).

CHANGED
- data-tooltip now matches LabelTooltip's dark chip (#262626/white, 6px radius) instead of a lighter bordered card.
- TableColumnFilter&lt;TItem&gt; lost its own FilterButtonLabelFormat/FilterAppliedButtonLabelFormat/FilterAppliedLabel/FilterLabel parameters -- the accessible name now comes from Table's parameters of the same names. Only affects code that instantiates TableColumnFilter directly.
- PropertyColumn&lt;TItem,TProp&gt; now annotates TProp with [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.All)]. Concrete TProp="..." markup is unaffected; a consumer generic forwarding its own unannotated TProp into PropertyColumn needs the same annotation to avoid IL2091 under trim analysis.

FIXED (all pre-existing, from the 10.6.7/10.7.0 column filtering -- not regressions in this release)
- Under ScrollY, the fixed-positioned filter dropdown stretched to the viewport's right edge -- the stylesheet's right: 0 anchor was never cleared.
- The filter dropdown was clipped by .wss-table-wrapper on a table short enough with no ScrollY; it escapes on every open now, not only under ScrollY.
- A runtime Column.FilterMultiple true -&gt; false flip left the earlier multi-key selection applied (two checked radios in one group); it trims to the first key.

Full changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>dcblakesley</Authors>
    <Company>WSS</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 WssBlazorControls</Copyright>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Include README and the package icon (license is declared via PackageLicenseExpression) -->
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
